DESCRIPTION >
    Wave 3 tier-3 row-pull. Single conversion row (LIMIT 1, most recent) for one
    distinct_id — the "conversion" half of getAttributionExplanation
    (api/lib/attribution-engine.js:1081-1108, queryName 'attribution_explain_conversion').
    Faithful 1:1 port; 13 columns in the SAME order the caller destructures at :1108:
      timestamp, conversion_value, utm_source, utm_medium, utm_campaign,
      first_touch_source, first_touch_medium, first_touch_campaign, ai_source,
      page_url, user_id, anonymous_id, ingestion_method.
    Typed-column translation (SCOPE_v3 §2.6): properties.site_id -> site_id, event ->
    event_type; utm_*, first_touch_*, ai_source, page_url, ingestion_method are typed
    columns. MONEY FIELD: conversion_value ported as toFloat64OrZero(toString(conversion_value))
    == the live HogQL toFloatOrZero(toString(properties.conversion_value)) (matches dash_stages/
    admin_preview_kpis convention). BAG FIELDS: user_id, anonymous_id are §2.6 bag keys read via
    JSONExtractString(properties, '<key>') — same as journey.pipe / dashboard_recent_activity_events.
    NOTE ('' vs NULL): JSONExtractString returns '' for an absent key where live HogQL
    properties.<key> returns NULL; the caller collapses both via `x || null` (:1114-1115), so the
    divergence is inert at the consumed level — flagged, not "fixed", to stay a faithful port.
    NOT YET PUSHED — authored only (token lacks WORKSPACE:DEPLOY); founder deploys.

NODE attribution_explain_conversion_node
SQL >
    %
    SELECT
        timestamp,
        toFloat64OrZero(toString(conversion_value)) AS conversion_value,
        utm_source,
        utm_medium,
        utm_campaign,
        first_touch_source,
        first_touch_medium,
        first_touch_campaign,
        ai_source,
        page_url,
        JSONExtractString(properties, 'user_id') AS user_id,
        JSONExtractString(properties, 'anonymous_id') AS anonymous_id,
        ingestion_method
    FROM events
    WHERE site_id = {{ String(site_id, required=True) }}
      AND event_type = '$conversion'
      AND distinct_id = {{ String(distinct_id, required=True) }}
    ORDER BY timestamp DESC
    LIMIT 1

TYPE endpoint
